{"type": "message", "id": "a8e4a974", "parentId": "bd9f0c1e", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T15:38:02.241Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_4f416ae9b74e4783b49fb269", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"Top Ten Most Challenged Books 2016 American Library Association\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 947,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5853031d5d9677c4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nList of most commonly challenged books in the United States - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5853031d5d9677c4\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_most_commonly_challenged_books_in_the_United_States\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1cd9ce9113517c02\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis list of the most commonly challenged books in the United States refers to books sought to be removed or otherwise restricted from public access, typically from a library or a school curriculum. This list is primarily based on U.S. data gathered by the American Library Association&#x27;s Office for Intellectual Freedom (OIF), which gathers data from media reports, and from reports from librarians and teachers. As of 2020, the top ten ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1cd9ce9113517c02\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 11, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f79394f25a4f501c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop 10 and Frequently Challenged Books Archive | Banned Books\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f79394f25a4f501c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ala.org/bbooks/frequentlychallengedbooks/top10/archive