an oral sex scene, and Eleanor and Park, by Rainbow Rowell, whcih has been challenged for numerous reasons, ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2ef4f3ac848879b5\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"August 3, 2024\",\n      \"siteName\": \"ncac.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e1207df3297f7ba3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop Ten Most Challenged Books 2016 — a community-created list from Chapel_Hill_Christine | The Seattle Public Library | BiblioCommons\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e1207df3297f7ba3\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://seattle.bibliocommons.com/v2/list/display/687698309/962792787\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"225b056517e86fc7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nEach year, the American Library Association&#x27;s Office for Intellectual Freedom posts a report of the ten most challenged books from the previous year. Use this list for inspiration to enter our Banned Books Trading Card Art Contest, and find previous years lists linked at the bottom!\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"225b056517e86fc7\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"seattle.bibliocommons.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b2d73c0578f96586\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nALA Top 10 Most Challenged Books | 2016 | Awards and Honors | LibraryThing\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b2d73c0578f96586\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.librarything.com/award/1636.0.0.2016/ALA-Top-10-Most-Challenged-Books-2016\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4873b3d82ba604b3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSurveys indicate that 82-97% of book challenges remain unreported and receive no media coverage. show less ... All, 2024 (10), 2023 (10), 2022 (13), 2021 (10), 2020 (10), 2019 (10), 2018 (11), 2017 (10), 2016 (10), 2015 (10), 2014 (10), 2013 (10), 2012 (10), 2011 (10), 2010 (10), 2009 (10), 2008 (10), 2007 (10), 2006 (10), 2005 (10), 2004 (10), 2003 (10), 2002 (10), 2001 (10) 20th century(3,466) adventure(4,546) Afghanistan(3,173) African American(2,718) American(3,574) American literature(5,384) autism(2,490) children(2,790) children&#x27;s(4,434) children&#x27;s literature(2,444) classic(9,824) classi\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4873b3d82ba604b3\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.librarything.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"831fe2c05c5f0aaa\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBanned Books Week: Top Ten Most Challenged Books of 2016 — a staff-created list from The Seattle Public Library | Chicago Public Library | BiblioCommons\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"831fe2c05c5f0aaa\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://chipublib.bibliocommons.com/v2/list/display/72450558/1057030297\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8fb9d0068d2ff9d4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIncluded on the National Book Award longlist and designated a Stonewall Honor Book, this young adult novel was challenged because its cover has an image of two boys kissing, and it was considered to include sexually explicit LGBT content. ... This 2006 Printz Award winner is a young adult novel that was challenged and restricted for a sexually explicit scene that may lead a student to “sexual experimentation.” ... Considered to be sexually explicit by library staff and administrators, this compilation of adult comic books by two prolific award-winning artists was banned and challenged.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8fb9d0068d2ff9d4\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"chipublib.bibliocommons.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"52bd0ec685f8045d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop Ten Challenged Books of 2016 - Intellectual Freedom Blog\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"52bd0ec685f8045d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https:/