{"type": "message", "id": "28ed68f2", "parentId": "0aea51bf", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T15:38:22.454Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "71f140c8aa9649f88977bdc855a200fb", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"Top Ten Challenged Books of 2017 American Library Association\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 980,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"51fc82cdf202db42\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNational Library Week: Top Ten Most Challenged Books of 2017 - Blog - Free Library\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"51fc82cdf202db42\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"http://libwww.library.phila.gov/blog/post/3296\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"80680521c77fd353\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTo Kill a Mockingbird by Harper Lee This Pulitzer Prize–winning novel, considered an American classic, was challenged and banned because of violence and its use of the N-word. The Hate U Give by Angie Thomas Despite winning multiple awards and being the most searched-for book on Goodreads during its debut year, this YA novel was challenged and banned in school libraries and curricula because it was considered &quot;pervasively vulgar&quot; and because of drug use, profanity, and offensive language.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"80680521c77fd353\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"libwww.library.phila.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2e7d9207cc690e11\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nList of most commonly challenged books in the United States - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2e7d9207cc690e11\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_most_commonly_challenged_books_in_the_United_States\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e658c211253d1055\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis list of the most commonly challenged books in the United States refers to books sought to be removed or otherwise restricted from public access, typically from a library or a school curriculum. This list is primarily based on U.S. data gathered by the American Library Association&#x27;s Office for Intellectual Freedom (OIF), which gathers data from media reports, and from reports from librarians and teachers. As of 2020, the top ten ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e658c211253d1055\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 11, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1e17b93260bf7400\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nALA Office for Intellectual Freedom Names Ten Most Challenged Books of 2017 | Banned Books Week\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1e17b93260bf7400\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://bannedbooksweek.org/ala-office-for-intellectual-freedom-names-ten-most-challenged-books-of-2017/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5c116d9ae92f873f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn recognition of National Library Week, the American Library Association’s Office for Intellectual Freedom (OIF) has published their annual list of the ten most frequently challenged and banned books, along with an analysis of the censorship threats facing U.S. schools and libraries. In 2017, ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5c116d9ae92f873f\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"bannedbooksweek.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9477ca8e0a5658a7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop 10 and Frequently Challenged Books Archive | Banned Books\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9477ca8e0a5658a7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ala.org/bbooks/frequentlychallengedbooks/top10/archive\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5830cbc19a4af3ea\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAnd Tango Makes Three written by Peter Parnell and Justin Richardson and illustrated by Henry Cole Returning after a brief hiatus from the Top Ten Most Challenged list, this ALA Notable Children’s Book, published in 2005, was challenged and labeled because it features a same-sex relationship. I Am Jazz written by Jessica Herthel and Jazz Jennings and illustrated by Shelagh McNicholas This autobiographical picture book co-written by the 13-year-old protagonist was challenged because it addresses gender identity. Download the Censorship by the Numbers 2017 infographic.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5830cbc19a4af3ea\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a94386e5d9d87e97\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nALA Announces Top Ten Challenged Books in 2017 | the American Booksellers Association\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a94386e5d9d87e97\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.bookweb.org/news/ala-announces-top-ten-challenged-books-2017-103841\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ae236d246f7fa715\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe American Library Association has released its list of the books that were most frequently banned or challenged in schools or libraries in 2017.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ae236d246f7fa715\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"July 11, 2018\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.bookweb.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"47861378d4830646\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop Ten Most Challenged Books Lists | Advocacy, Legislation & Issues\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"47861378d4830646\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://web.archive.org/web/20170728055307/http:/www.ala.org:80/advocacy/bbooks/frequentlychallengedbooks/top10\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"55ce52f6acb6add5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nYou are at: ALA.org » ADVOCACY » BBOOKS » Frequently Challenged Books » Top Ten Most Challenged Books Lists ... The American Library Association condemns censorship and works to ensure free access to information. Every year, the Office for Intellectual Freedom (OIF) compiles a list of the Top Ten Most Challenged Books in order to inform the public about censorship in libraries and schools.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"55ce52f6acb6add5\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"July 18, 2017\",\n      \"siteName\": \"web.archive.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4a1e29f767ed8b1c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nALA Announces 2017's Top 10 Most-Challenged Books\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4a1e29f767ed8b1c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://bookriot.com/ala-2017-most-challenged-books/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"674e1f2069ba5c91\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe ALA shares last year&#x27;s most-challenged books, including two by men who have been accused of sexual misconduct. Annika Barranti Klein Apr 10, 2018 · This content contains affiliate links. When you buy through these links, we may earn an affiliate commission. Staff Writer · Annika Barranti Klein likes books, obviously. Twitter: @noirbettie · View All posts by Annika Barranti Klein · The American Library Association announced the Top 10 Most-Challenged Books of 2017 yesterday: View this post on Instagram ·\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"674e1f2069ba5c91\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 11, 2018\",\n      \"siteName\": \"bookriot.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c10601962557fc01\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe 10 Most Challenged Books Of 2017, According To The American Library Association [via Bustle] The American Library... – @cheshirelibrary on Tumblr\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c10601962557fc01\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.tumblr.com/cheshirelibrary/172866029663/the-10-most-challenged-books-of-2017-according-to\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e793dfa57ef8fe76\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nReturning after a brief hiatus from the Top Ten Most Challenged list, this ALA Notable Children’s Book, published in 2005, was challenged and labeled because it features a same-sex relationship. 10. I Am Jazz written by Jessica Herthel and Jazz Jennings and illustrated by Shelagh McNicholas · This autobiographical picture book co-written by the 13-year-old protagonist was challenged because it addresses gender identity. #cheshire library#american library association#banned books#challenged books#national library week\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e793dfa57ef8fe76\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.tumblr.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3c19c46dbf552b1b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop 10 Most Challenged Books of 2024 | Banned Books\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3c19c46dbf552b1b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ala.org/bbooks/frequentlychallengedbooks/top10\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8e17bf587d2ce632\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nEvery year, the American Library Association compiles a list of the Top 10 Most Frequently Challenged Books based on reports from the field and media coverage.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8e17bf587d2ce632\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.ala.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dd7c30095f3fd1aa\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBanned & Challenged Books | Banned Books\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dd7c30095f3fd1aa\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ala.org/bbooks\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d656b6b1bc85164f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nALA compiled data on censorship attempts in libraries and schools during 2024. ... Learn about the most challenged books of 2024.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d656b6b1bc85164f\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.ala.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "Top Ten Challenged Books of 2017 American Library Association", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 980, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"51fc82cdf202db42\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNational Library Week: Top Ten Most Challenged Books of 2017 - Blog - Free Library\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"51fc82cdf202db42\">>>", "url": "http://libwww.library.phila.gov/blog/post/3296", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"80680521c77fd353\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTo Kill a Mockingbird by Harper Lee This Pulitzer Prize–winning novel, considered an American classic, was challenged and banned because of violence and its use of the N-word. The Hate U Give by Angie Thomas Despite winning multiple awards and being the most searched-for book on Goodreads during its debut year, this YA novel was challenged and banned in school libraries and curricula because it was considered &quot;pervasively vulgar&quot; and because of drug use, profanity, and offensive language.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"80680521c77fd353\">>>", "siteName": "libwww.library.phila.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2e7d9207cc690e11\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nList of most commonly challenged books in the United States - Wikipedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2e7d9207cc690e11\">>>", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_most_commonly_challenged_books_in_the_United_States", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e658c211253d1055\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThis list of the most commonly challenged books in the United States refers to books sought to be removed or otherwise restricted from public access, typically from a library or a school curriculum. This list is primarily based on U.S. data gathered by the American Library Association&#x27;s Office for Intellectual Freedom (OIF), which gathers data from media reports, and from reports from librarians and teachers. As of 2020, the top ten ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"e658c211253d1055\">>>", "published": "February 11, 2026", "siteName": "en.wikipedia.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1e17b93260bf7400\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nALA Office for Intellectual Freedom Names Ten Most Challenged Books of 2017 | Banned Books Week\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1e17b93260bf7400\">>>", "url": "https://bannedbooksweek.org/ala-office-for-intellectual-freedom-names-ten-most-challenged-books-of-2017/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5c116d9ae92f873f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn recognition of National Library Week, the American Library Association’s Office for Intellectual Freedom (OIF) has published their annual list of the ten most frequently challenged and banned books, along with an analysis of the censorship threats facing U.S. schools and libraries. In 2017, ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5c116d9ae92f873f\">>>", "siteName": "bannedbooksweek.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9477ca8e0a5658a7\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTop 10 and Frequently Challenged Books Archive | Banned Books\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9477ca8e0a5658a7\">>>", "url": "https://www.ala.org/bbooks/frequentlychallengedbooks/top10/archive", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5830cbc19a4af3ea\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAnd Tango Makes Three written by Peter Parnell and Justin Richardson and illustrated by Henry Cole Returning after a brief hiatus from the Top Ten Most Challenged list, this ALA Notable Children’s Book, published in 2005, was challenged and labeled because it features a same-sex relationship. I Am Jazz written by Jessica Herthel and Jazz Jennings and illustrated by Shelagh McNicholas This autobiographical picture book co-written by the 13-year-old protagonist was challenged because it addresses gender identity. Download the Censorship by the Numbers 2017 infographic.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5830cbc19a4af3ea\">>>", "siteName": "www.ala.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a94386e5d9d87e97\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nALA Announces Top Ten Challenged Books in 2017 | the American Booksellers Association\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a94386e5d9d87e97\">>>", "url": "https://www.bookweb.org/news/ala-announces-top-ten-challenged-books-2017-103841", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ae236d246f7fa715\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe American Library Association has released its list of the books that were most frequently banned or challenged in schools or libraries in 2017.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ae236d246f7fa715\">>>", "published": "July 11, 2018", "siteName": "www.bookweb.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"47861378d4830646\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTop Ten Most Challenged Books Lists | Advocacy, Legislation & Issues\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"47861378d4830646\">>>", "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20170728055307/http:/www.ala.org:80/advocacy/bbooks/frequentlychallengedbooks/top10", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"55ce52f6acb6add5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nYou are at: ALA.org » ADVOCACY » BBOOKS » Frequently Challenged Books » Top Ten Most Challenged Books Lists ... The American Library Association condemns censorship and works to ensure free access to inf