st Banned &amp; Challenged Books of 2019 by DRMoon_Staff - a staff-created list : This year, according to the ALA&#x27;s website, the Office of Intellectual Freedom tracked &quot;377 challenges to library, school, and university materials and services in 2019. Of 566 books that were targeted, here are the most challenged, along with the reasons cited for censoring the books&quot;.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6af999c37ace3d55\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"more.bibliocommons.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f18d2dc804a431d3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nALA Top 10 Most Challenged Books | 2019 | Awards and Honors | LibraryThing\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f18d2dc804a431d3\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.librarything.com/award/1636.0.0.2019/ALA-Top-10-Most-Challenged-Books-2019\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"043ad0ad7a001de8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\ngrrlofhighart (100 works), Kaethe (86), VadersMorwen (83), RLNunezKPL (74), angieunplugged (72), e-zReader (70), saraparris (68), 0x0axd (67), Pages_Aplenty (64), tasslyn (64), NikNak73 (63), snicklefritzsass (62), kwagnerroberts (61), t4becker (59), lmackiewicz (57), kpaixao (56), Spoto-Media (56), kday_working (55), prengel90 (54), pollyalida (53), sandmanbooks (53), simonamitac (53), Sullywriter (53), test_logo_exist_lt (53), HCLibrary (52), pricem (52), alaskabookworm (51), griffinel (51), tarr.chris (51), kateykayy (50), KeithKron (50), sisypheand (50), xofelf (50), ALA_Banned_Books (49),\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"043ad0ad7a001de8\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.librarything.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dad293406744d372\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop 10 Challenged Books of 2019\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dad293406744d372\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.publishersweekly.com/pw/by-topic/childrens/childrens-industry-news/article/83105-top-10-challenged-books-of-2019.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7836ee32508c519e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn honor of National Library Week, April 19–25, the American Library Association has released its annual report on nationwide library trends, statistics, and issues, including the ALA Office for Intellectual Freedom’s list of Top 10 Most Challenged Books of 2019.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7836ee32508c519e\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 20, 2020\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.publishersweekly.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3700c2876db140f2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nALA Posts “Top 10 Most Challenged Books in 2019”\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3700c2876db140f2\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.infodocket.com/2020/04/20/ala-releases-most-frequently-challenged-books-of-2019-list/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"02709e92fed6c69f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nHere are the “Top 10 Most Challenged Books in 2019,” along with the reasons cited for censoring the books: ... Reasons: to avoid controversy; for LGBTQIA+ content and a transgender character; because schools and libraries should not “put books in a child’s hand that require discussion”; for sexual references; and for conflicting with a religious viewpoint and “traditional family structure”\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"02709e92fed6c69f\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 20, 2020\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.infodocket.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0b316c13ed0d5fe0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2019 - Banned Books - CEFLS at Clinton Essex Franklin Library System\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0b316c13ed0d5fe0\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://cefls.libguides.com/banned-books/2019\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ba9d52422ffe8661\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nA resource pertaining to banned and challenged books. The American Library Association&#x27;s top ten most challenged books from 2019.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ba9d52422ffe8661\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 23, 2024\",\n      \"siteName\": \"cefls.libguides.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3cf69c1429bb0104\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop 10 Most Challenged Books of 2019 » NCW Libraries home %\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3cf69c1429bb0104\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ncwlibraries.org/top-10-most-challenged-books-of-2019/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"352e982222d2c9bc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nEvery year the American Library Association’s Office for Intellectual Freedom compiles a list of the Top 10 Most Challenged books in order to inform the public about censorship in libraries and schools. The lists are based on information from media stories and voluntary reports sent to OIF ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"352e982222d2c9bc\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 17, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.ncwlibraries.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"181413a98dc320c4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTop Ten Most Banned & Challenged Books of 2019 — a staff-created list from MORE Libraries | MORE Libraries | BiblioCommons\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"181413a98dc320c4\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://more.bibliocommons.com/v2/list/display/1537348899/1624720941\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"234fd6906b155ec6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>a Book About Bodies, Feelings, and YOU</strong>Silverberg, Cory, ... Reasons: Challenged, banned, and relocated for LGBTQIA+ content; for discussing gender identity and sex education; and for concerns that the title and illustrations were “inappropriate”\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"234fd6906b155ec6\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 23, 2026\",\n      \"siteName\": \"more.bibliocommons.com\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "Top Ten Challenged Books of 2019 American Library Association", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 950, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"14ce795342bcc38d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTop 10 Most Challenged Books of 2019 - National Coalition Against Censorship\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"14ce795342bcc38d\">>>", "url": "https://ncac.org/banned-books-week/banned-books-top-10", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d3fc462910388d6c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAnd Tango Makes Three by Peter Parnell and Justin Richardson illustrated by Henry Cole Reason: Challenged and relocated for LGBTQIA+ content · Graphics created by the American Library Association Office for Intellectual Freedom ... Our colleagues at the American Library Association (ALA) this week released their annual list of the ten most…\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d3fc462910388d6c\">>>", "published": "August 24, 2024", "siteName": "ncac.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"902c4bdf00ed15cb\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nA Day in the Life of... ALA's Top 10 Most Challenged Books - Intellectual Freedom Blog\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"902c4bdf00ed15cb\">>>", "url": "https://www.oif.ala.org/a-day-in-the-life-of-alas-top-10-most-challenged-books/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a5b56b9ee19d10ff\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nDuring National Library Week, the Office for Intellectual Freedom discusses the past year&#x27;s trends. Of the 566 books that were targeted in 2019, here are the most challenged, along with the reasons cited for censoring the books.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a5b56b9ee19d10ff\">>>", "published": "October 30, 2020", "siteName": "www.oif.ala.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ea0af27606ca1156\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nList of most commonly challenged books in the United States - Wikipedia\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ea0af27606ca1156\">>>", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_most_commonly_challenged_books_in_the_United_States", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b8f9557a8de2aca8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThis list of the most commonly challenged books in the United States refers to books sought to be removed or otherwise restricted from public access, typically from a library or a school curriculum. This list is primarily based on U.S. data gathered by the American Library Association&#x27;s Office for Intellectual Freedom (OIF), which gathers data from media reports, and from reports from librarians and teachers. As of 2020, the top ten ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b8f9557a8de2aca8\">>>", "published": "February 11, 2026", "siteName": "en.wikipedia.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cc83000297e9f260\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTop Ten Most Banned & Challenged Books of 2019 | MORE Libraries | BiblioCommons\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"cc83000297e9f260\">>>", "url": "https://more.bibliocommons.com/list/share/1537348899/1624720941", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6af999c37ace3d55\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTop Ten Most Banned &amp; Challenged Books of 2019 by DRMoon_Staff - a staff-created list : This year, according to the ALA&#x27;s website, the Office of Intellectual Freedom tracked &quot;377 challenges to library, school, and university materials and services in 2019. Of 566 books that were targeted, here are the most challenged, along with the reasons cited for censoring the books&quot;.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6af999c37ace3d55\">>>", "siteName": "more.bibliocommons.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f18d2dc804a431d3\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nALA Top 10 Most Challenged Books | 2019 | Awards and Honors | LibraryThing\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f18d2dc804a431d3\">>>", "url": "https://www.librarything.com/award/1636.0.0.2019/ALA-Top-10-Most-Challenged-Books-2019", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"043ad0ad7a001de8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\ngrrlofhighart (100 works), Kaethe (86), VadersMorwen (83), RLNunezKPL (74), angieunplugged (72), e-zReader (70), saraparris (68), 0x0axd (67), Pages_Aplenty (64), tasslyn (64), NikNak73 (63), snicklefritzsass (62), kwagnerroberts (61), t4becker (59), lmackiewicz (57), kpaixao (56), Spoto-Media (56), kday_working (55), prengel90 (54), pollyalida (53), sandmanbooks (53), simonamitac (53), Sullywriter (53), test_logo_exist_lt (53), HCLibrary (52), pricem (52), alaskabookworm (51), griffinel (51), tarr.chris (51), kateykayy (50), KeithKron (50), sisypheand (50), xofelf (50), ALA_Banned_Books (49),\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"043ad0ad7a001de8\">>>", "siteName": "www.librarything.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dad293406744d372\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTop 10 Challenged Books of 2019\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dad293406744d372\">>>", "url": "https://www.publishersweekly.com/pw/by-topic/childrens/childrens-industry-news/article/83105-top-10-challenged-books-of-2019.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7836ee32508c519e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn honor of National Library Week, April 19–25, the American Library Association has released its annual report on nationwide library trends, statistics, and issues, including the ALA Office for Intellectual Freedom’s list of Top 10 Most Challenged Books of 2019.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7836ee32508c519e\">>>", "published": "April 20, 2020", "siteName": "www.publishersweekly.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3700c2876db140f2\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nALA Posts “Top 10 Most Challenged Books in 2019”\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3700c2876db140f2\">>>", "url": "https://www.infodocket.com/2020/04/20/ala-releases-most-frequently-challenged-books-of-2019-list/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"02709e92fed6c69f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nHere are the “Top 10 Most Challenged Books in 2019,” along with the reasons cited for censoring the books: ... Reasons: to avoid controversy; for LGBTQIA+ content and a transgender character; because schools and libraries should not “put books in a child’s hand that require discussion”; for sexual references; and for conflicting with a religious viewpoint and “traditional family structure”\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"02709e92fed6c69f\">>>", "published": "April 20, 2020", "siteName": "www.infodocket.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0b316c13ed0d5fe0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2019 - Banned Books - CEFLS at Clinton Essex Franklin Library System\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0b316c13ed0d5fe0\">>>", "url": "https://cefls.libguides.com/banned-books/2019", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ba9d52422ffe8661\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nA resource pertaining to banned and challenged books. The American Library Association&#x27;s top ten most challenged books from 2019.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ba9d52422ffe8661\">>>", "published": "October 23, 2024", "siteName": "cefls.libguides.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3cf69c1429bb0104\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTop 10 Most Challenged Books of 2019 » NCW Libraries home %\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3cf69c1429bb0104\">>>", "url": "https://www.ncwlibraries.org/top-10-most-challenged-books-of-2019/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"352e982222d2c9bc\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nEvery year the American Library Association’s Office for Intellectual Freedom compiles a list of the Top 10 Most Challenged books in order to inform the public about censorship in libraries and schools. The lists are based on information from media stories and voluntary reports sent to OIF ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"352e982222d2c9bc\">>>", "published": "October 17, 2025", "siteName": "www.ncwlibraries.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"181413a98dc320c4\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTop Ten Most Banned & Challenged Books of 2019 — a staff-created list from MORE Libraries | MORE Libraries | BiblioCommons\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"181413a98dc320c4\">>>", "url": "https://more.bibliocommons.com/v2/list/display/1537348899/1624720941", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"234fd6906b155ec6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n<strong>a Book About Bodies, Feelings, and YOU</strong>Silverberg, Cory, ... Reasons: Challenged, banned, and relocated for LGBTQIA+ content; for discussing gender identity and sex education; and for concerns that the title and illustrations were “inappropriate”\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"234fd6906b155ec6\">>>", "published": "February 23, 2026", "siteName": "more.bibliocommons.com"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775749134968}}
